# Schemathesis fuzz-gate ignore-list (issue #369).
#
# The Schemathesis workflow (schemathesis.yml) derives request cases from
# backend/openapi.yaml and gates on two failure classes — 5xx responses
# (`not_a_server_error`) and auth-protected operations that return data without
# auth (`ignored_auth`) — enforced by backend/cmd/schemagate, in the same
# "ignore-list with justification" shape as zap/dast.ignore and
# docker/cis-hardening.ignore. Conformance noise (undocumented status codes,
# content-type/schema drift, unsupported methods) is reported but never gated;
# it does not belong here.
#
# Format: one rule per line,
#
#   <kind> <operation-regex>   # justification
#
# where <kind> is one of `server_error` (a 5xx), `auth` (an ignored-auth
# finding), or `*` (both), and <operation-regex> is a Go regexp matched against
# the Schemathesis operation label (`METHOD /path`, e.g. `POST /contacts`). A
# `#` begins a comment; a trailing comment on a rule is its justification and
# is logged on every [ACCEPT].
#
# Every entry must carry a justification — an accepted finding is a written-down
# decision, not a silenced one. Re-run the gate locally before adding an entry:
# the finding must be reproducible, understood, and genuinely out of the gate's
# scope (e.g. a multipart upload handler that cannot accept a fuzzed body).
#
# No entries yet: as of this writing, both the anonymous and authenticated
# fuzz runs complete with zero 5xx and zero ignored-auth findings.
